  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alaska has accumulated $3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations count reached 8,338 awards, with an average award size of $364K. Obligations fell 21.2% year over year. Historical totals show growth through FY25, with FY21 at $2.3B, FY22 at $3.3B, FY23 at $3.8B, FY24 at $3.8B, FY25 at $3.9B, and a partial FY26 at $3B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B so far. The Department of Homeland Security and the General Services Administration follow with $562M and $493M in obligations respectively. Construction-related industries lead sector spending: Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $955M. Pharmacy benefit management and related services shows $261M in obligations, matching the top vendor TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $261M. DAVIS CONSTRUCTORS & ENGINEERS, INC. is the top vendor with $470M. The note on totals: these figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Alaska changed recently?",
        "body": "Federal contract obligations in Alaska fell 21.2% year over year. Obligations reached $3B in FY2026 to date after a peak of $3.9B in FY25 and steady totals of $3.8B in FY23 and FY24. Award activity includes 8,338 contracts with an average award size of $364K. These figures reflect partial fiscal-year totals for FY2026."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for the most spending in Alaska?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B in FY2026 to date, the largest agency buyer. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $562M and the General Services Administration obligated $493M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries with $955M, and Pharmacy Benefit Management and related services accounts for $261M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Alaska?",
      "a": "Alaska receives $3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total obligations are based on 8,338 awards with an average award size of $364K, and obligations fell 21.2% year over year. Historical annual obligations were $2.3B in FY21, $3.3B in FY22, $3.8B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, and $3.9B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Alaska?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Alaska. The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $562M and the General Services Administration at $493M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Alaska?",
      "a": "The largest federal contractors in Alaska are DAVIS CONSTRUCTORS & ENGINEERS, INC. with $470M and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $261M. TUTOR PERINI CORPORATION is third with $225M, followed by ASRC BUILDERS-CADDELL, LLC at $129M and JAG KETCHIKAN, LLC at $108M."
